As I was trying for the umteenth time to roll up a suitable starting
character it occured to me that it probably wouldn't be too hard to
make a patch that would do it auto-magically.  What I am thinking of
would not be a super powerful character but a real loser. The "loser"
patch would make the starting stats low across the board and assure
low INT and WIS for spellcasters or low STR, CON and DEX for the
rest. The loser would start with even worse equipment. For instance, a
simple cloak instead of magic resistance for wizards, no enchantment
on the staff and only one random non-attack spell. Finally, negative
luck and an angry god just to add to the challenge. A variation that
could be fun would be the "nerd" patch for a brainy barbarian.

Anyway the start up screen could be changed to something like
this:

Your brother, a newly trained Gallant, was heralded
from birth as the instrument of Lugh.  He was destined
to recover the Amulet for his deity, or die in the
attempt.  Unfortunately he died rescuing you once agian.
Lugh has demanded that YOU shall recover the amulet or, 
in your case, get killed trying. Your hour of destiny 
has come.  For the sake of us all:  Go bravely with 
the wrath of Lugh! 

For the Quest a message could be added such as:

The Green Wizard looks at you and sighs the says
"So it has come to this, I must depend on the likes
